(footprint "SW_Taiway_200_DPDT"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Taiway series 200 sub-miniature DPDT toggle, PCB vertical, M2 PC thru-hole. Fits any 200-MDPx: ON-ON, ON-OFF-ON, or the custom MDP6 ON-ON-ON. Terminals on a 2.54 x 5.08 grid, 10-48 UNS bushing (o4.80 thread, 5.50 high, flat) -> o4.95 panel hole. Body 8.10 (throw axis, X) x 9.10. PADS ARE NUMBERED AS THE DATASHEET DOES: pins 1-2-3 are one pole and 4-5-6 the other, with the COMMONS on 2 and 5, i.e. the centre of each row. Taiway's contact table is written in this numbering (ON-ON-ON reads 2-3,5-6 / 2-3,5-4 / 2-1,5-4), so a symbol drawn from the datasheet drops straight on. Two variants are in circulation and both disagree with the datasheet: one mirrored to 3-2-1 / 6-5-4, and one with the commons remapped onto pads 1 and 4. If a design needs a patched symbol to make this switch work, it has a mis-numbered footprint, not a symbol problem. The test that survives any rotation: walking 1-2-3-6-5-4 traces a CLOCKWISE loop seen from the component side.")
	(tags "toggle switch dpdt on-on-on on-off-on subminiature taiway 200 eurorack")
